# The enters trigger is independent of its source once triggered (CR 113.7a, 603.4, 608.2h): Doomsday Excruciator is cast on
# turn 3 (Mox Jet's {B}, Dark Ritual, Black Lotus), and with the trigger on the stack Bot2 exiles it with Swords to Plowshares
# (Bot1 gains 6, 26). "If it was cast" was true as it entered, so the trigger still resolves, from last-known information: every
# library is cut to its bottom six. Bot1's library of nine (after the turn-3 draw) loses three Swamps, Bot2's of twelve loses six
# Islands: nine cards face down, plus the Excruciator itself face up (Swords exiles it normally) is ten in exile. No upkeep draw
# ever happens: it never reaches an upkeep.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Dark Ritual
Black Lotus
Doomsday Excruciator
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Swords to Plowshares
Island x18

